    <h2>The honest answer</h2>
    <p><strong>If you are a design-led business (photographer, boutique, restaurant, wedding venue) without complex local-SEO needs, Squarespace is genuinely a good fit.</strong> The platform was built for your use case.</p>
    <p><strong>If you are a service business that lives or dies on local search (HVAC, plumbing, roofing, electrical, contractors, inspectors), Squarespace's SEO ceiling is real.</strong> The page-speed gap and the shallow schema add up to fewer calls. A custom build pays for itself in 6&ndash;18 months for any service business doing more than 20&ndash;30 jobs a month.</p>
